sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant S as Scheduler (skins.price_sync, every 5 min)
    participant WP as Waxpeer
    participant DB as Postgres
    participant R as Redis

    S->>S: skip unless sync enabled and key set
    S->>WP: GET /v1/prices/snapshot?format=csv (streamed)
    WP-->>S: ~1.2 M rows (item_id, name, price, auto)
    S->>S: aggregate to one row per (name, phase), only auto listings set a price
    S->>WP: GET /v1/prices?minified=0 (type, rarity, image for new names)
    WP-->>S: names with taxonomy
    S->>DB: count active rows
    alt names with an auto listing fewer than half of the active catalogue
        S->>R: skins:job:price_sync = {ok: false, error: thin_snapshot}
        Note over S,DB: refused before any lock or write, previous prices stand
    else normal snapshot
        S->>DB: advisory xact lock (pricing)
        S->>DB: apply: update rows whose price_hash changed, deactivate absent rows, insert stubs
        S->>DB: reprice all active rows (rules read fresh from Postgres) -> sell_price_usd, discount_percent
        S->>DB: COMMIT
        S->>R: INCR skins:catalog:ver (cached pages expire)
        S->>R: skins:job:price_sync = {ok: true, changed, deactivated, stubs}
    end
    Note over S,WP: A Waxpeer error or crash is logged by exception type name only and recorded as ok: false
